#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script --quiet
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.12,<3.13"
# dependencies = ["pydantic>=2.14", "httpx>=0.28.1"]
# ///
"""vfg: the one command every agent on the owner's PC uses to reach the EC2 box.

Run by uv (the lines above) on Python 3.12 with pydantic, which the actions need: the one
loader, lib/py/vfg_actions.py, is imported only by the commands that use the actions, so the
others start as fast as before. Run as `python3 vfg` where pydantic is missing, it starts
itself again under uv. Every remote action is one SSH call whose
remote command is the box's Python 3.12, `/opt/vfg/python/bin/python3 -u -` (VFG_REMOTE_VFG's
python/bin/python3), with remote/common.py, a line
`ARGS = json.loads(...)`, any library it uses (scripts/_lib/places.py) as a module of
its own, and one program from remote/ on its stdin, so nothing an agent typed
ever meets a shell on either machine. The one exception is
`vfg feed post`, whose remote command the contract fixes (with VFG_DB and
VFG_FEED set in front through `env`); it is built with shlex.join. See README.md.
"""
